RESEARCHER [research]
NVIDIA recently announced its financial results for the third quarter of fiscal 2024, which ended on October 29, 2023. The company reported a revenue of **$18.12 billion**, marking a **206% increase** from the same quarter last year and a **34% increase** from the previous quarter ([source](https://investor.nvidia.com/news/press-release-details/2023/NVIDIA-Announces-Financial-Results-for-Third-Quarter-Fiscal-2024/default.aspx)). 

In terms of earnings per share, GAAP earnings were **$0.27**, down **72%** from a year ago but up **4%** from the previous quarter. Non-GAAP earnings were **$0.58**, down **50%** from a year ago and up **14%** from the previous quarter ([source](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581022000163/q3fy23pr.htm)).

Overall, the sentiment surrounding NVIDIA's earnings report appears to be positive, given the significant revenue growth and the company's ability to adapt to market conditions, despite the decline in earnings per share. 

For further details, you can refer to the official press release [here](https://investor.nvidia.com/news/press-release-details/2023/NVIDIA-Announces-Financial-Results-for-Third-Quarter-Fiscal-2024/default.aspx).

SUPERVISOR [route]
